F = {
 "bg|Shadowmoor Expert": "You know Shadowmoor, a dim and unruly land lit only by pale moonlight, either by birth or long study. Surviving there takes sharp wits or sheer courage. Life taught you that trust is scarce, and that choosing wrongly who to rely on can cost you everything.",
 "bg|Shipwright": "You have spent your life around ships and the water you love. You fought in a war aboard great vessels and kept their hulls afloat with whatever you had. You also helped build a fishing boat that rescued a starving town, and you still dream of a prow you cannot carve.",
 "bg|Silverquill Student": "You trained for years in writing and public speaking to earn a place at Silverquill College. Your studies center on language, literature, and the force of words. You learned that speech can reveal or hide the truth, and that magic can do the same in earnest.",
 "bg|Simic Scientist": "You work in the Simic Combine laboratories, trying to grow a world where nature and cities fit together. You believe life must adapt, and that biomancers should help it keep pace with civilization. If your experiments also yield monstrous soldiers to defend the Combine against rival guilds, all the better.",
 "bg|Smuggler": "You move goods that others want hidden. You once floated a hundred swords past careless dock guards in fish barrels, and sold stolen elven wine at double its worth after a night on the river. At kinder moments, you carried refugees out of war zones or led herds away from fire.",
 "bg|Soldier": "War has shaped your life since youth. You learned weapons, armor, and how to stay alive on a battlefield. You may have served in a national army, a mercenary company, or a local militia that rose in a recent conflict. Work with your DM on your unit and rank.",
 "bg|Spellfire Initiate": "You carry spellfire, a rare gift that draws raw power from the Weave. Using it strains the body badly. To handle this sacred force safely, you have trained both your mind and your body with great discipline.",
 "bg|Spirit Medium": "Through odd rituals and chance meetings, you learned that you can link with the spirits of the dead and the damned. Your body lets them speak, and they sometimes grant you foresight. Their motives are not always kind, and their help leaves a lingering cost.",
 "bg|Urban Bounty Hunter": "You earned your living tracking people for pay, but in the city rather than the wilds. You deal with criminals and rival hunters alike and keep contacts in both circles. You might be a rooftop thief-catcher, a street-wise informant, or a hunter who mingles with nobles.",
 "bg|Urchin": "You grew up poor and alone on the streets, with no one to feed or protect you. You fought for scraps, slept on rooftops, and learned to watch for thieves. You survived through cunning, speed, strength, or all three, and now have enough coin to live modestly for ten days.",
 "bg|Uthgardt Tribe Member": "You come from an Uthgardt tribe, where cooperation and old traditions kept your people strong while other kingdoms fell. Some bands settled and traded, but the totems of Uthgar called many back to the old ways. You may be adrift from a settled tribe or seek glory for a traditional one.",
 "bg|Vampire Devotee": "You served a vampire or a small group of them who shared a lair. They fed on your blood many times. You may have served eagerly, hoping to become a vampire yourself, or been charmed and left with fuzzy memories. Either way, that life has ended.",
 "bg|Vampire Survivor": "You saw a vampire attack or lived through one. You may have fought in it or stood frozen in fear. Since then you stay alert for monsters and take pride in being prepared, so no vampire will surprise you or your friends again.",
 "bg|Variant City Watch (Investigator)": "You belonged to the rarer branch of a community's watch, the investigators who solve crimes after they happen. Most settlements of decent size have one or two who can read a crime scene and trail a culprit. You are skilled in Investigation rather than Athletics.",
 "bg|Variant Criminal (Spy)": "Your talents resemble those of a burglar or smuggler, but you honed them as an espionage agent. You may have worked as a sanctioned agent of the crown. Or you may have sold the secrets you uncovered to whoever paid the most.",
 "bg|Variant Entertainer (Gladiator)": "You turned combat into a show the crowd could enjoy, much like a minstrel or circus performer. You may also tumble or act. You can find work in any place that stages fights, such as an arena or a secret pit club, and may carry an unusual weapon like a trident or net.",
 "bg|Variant Guild Artisan (Guild Merchant)": "Rather than craft goods, you belong to a guild of traders, caravan masters, or shopkeepers. You earn your living by buying and selling what artisans make, or the materials they need. You may have hauled cargo by ship, wagon, or caravan, or run a small shop of your own.",
 "bg|Variant Noble (Knight)": "A knighthood is a modest noble rank, but it can lead higher. If you take this path, you gain retainers instead of a privileged position. One is a noble squire learning from you, while others might tend your horse or armor. You may carry a token from a lord or lady you admire.",
 "bg|Variant Sailor (Pirate)": "You spent your youth serving a ruthless pirate captain who taught you how to survive among sharks and savages. You have robbed on the high seas and sent deserving people to watery graves. Many port towns know your unsavory name, and you may take Bad Reputation instead of Ship's Passage.",
 "bg|Vizier": "You serve your god as a vizier, handling the tasks that help initiates on their journey. In return, the gods let you into the afterlife with the God-Pharaoh's blessing. You hope to be the finest servant possible. Most viziers are clerics, druids, or paladins.",
 "bg|Volstrucker Agent": "You belong to the Volstrucker, a secret order of arcane assassins serving the Cerberus Assembly. People in Dwendalian cities whisper of them as scourgers. Your duty is to silence those who threaten King Dwendal and the Assembly. The order recruits talented people already broken by tragedy.",
 "bg|Ward of the Sheltering Hands": "Bad luck brought you to the Sheltering Hands, a kind organization that defends the downtrodden. It helped you get back on your feet and taught you some protective magic. Its members hope you will one day shelter others in need.",
 "bg|Waterdhavian Noble": "You come from one of Waterdeep's great noble families, known across Faerun as eccentric, spoiled, and very rich. People expect certain things from your surname. You may be the rebel who prefers dungeons to balls, or a champion defending your family's legacy, and you might belong to a main line or a cousin branch.",
 "bg|Wayfarer": "You grew up on the streets among other unlucky castoffs, some friends and some rivals. You slept wherever you could and took odd jobs for food, and sometimes stole when hunger grew too sharp. Through it all you kept your pride and hope, because fate is not done with you.",
 "bg|Wildspacer": "You were raised in Wildspace, among asteroid miners, moon farmers, and other hardy folk. You may come from a distant settlement like the Rock of Bral, or have worked a spelljamming ship loading cargo and scraping the hull. That life has made you brave against the dangers of airless space.",
 "bg|Witchlight Hand": "As a youth you slipped into the Witchlight Carnival and stayed, working behind the scenes with the other hands. The carnival visits many worlds, but you see little of them. You barely know its owners, Mister Witch and Mister Light. The routine now feels dull, and bigger adventures may wait beyond its gates.",
 "bg|Witherbloom Student": "As a child you tried simple alchemy, hoping to enter Witherbloom College. Your reading centers on the life sciences, including biology and necromancy. Brewing odd medicinal mixtures, studying monster anatomy, and cataloging swamp plants are the studies you might pursue there.",
 "bg|Zhentarim Mercenary": "Maybe you needed coin, wanted a family, or just excel at getting jobs done by any means. You joined the Zhentarim, the Realms' most notorious mercenary guild. Its leaders call it a family, though it is full of dishonesty and corruption. You sharpened your cunning, reflexes, and blade to rise through its ranks.",
 "class|Artificer": "Artificers are inventors who use ingenuity and magic to give objects remarkable abilities. They treat magic as a complex system to be decoded and then put to use in spells and devices. This chapter holds all you need to play one.",
 "class|Barbarian": "Barbarians are defined by rage, a wild fury that can feel like a cornered predator, a storm, or a churning sea. Some draw it from animal spirits, others from anger at a painful world. It fuels their battle frenzy, reflexes, and strength, and they distrust the soft walls of civilization.",
 "class|Bard": "Bards weave magic through words and music, whether as scholars, skalds, or scoundrels. They inspire allies, shake foes, sway minds, make illusions, and heal wounds. Many believe the universe was spoken into being, and their songs capture echoes of that creation. Their great strength is versatility.",
 "class|Cleric": "Clerics link the mortal world to the planes of the gods and carry divine magic. They try to embody the work of the deity they serve. Their power comes from devotion, not study. They heal and inspire allies and also curse, terrify, and burn foes.",
 "class|Druid": "Druids revere nature and draw their magic from it or from a nature deity. They see themselves as extensions of its will, not its masters. Many follow the Old Faith, a mystic union with the wild. Their spells call on beasts, sun, moon, fire, and storm, and they can take animal forms.",
 "class|Fighter": "Fighters are the most varied class, from questing knights and royal champions to mercenaries and bandit kings. They share unmatched skill with weapons and armor and a deep knowledge of combat. They know death well, both dealing it and facing it unflinching. Each fighter learns the basics of every fighting style.",
 "class|Monk": "Monks magically harness the energy in their bodies, which most traditions call ki. They use it for striking combat skill or for subtler defense and speed. This power lets them create magical effects and surpass normal physical limits, and some of their attacks can disrupt an enemy's ki.",
 "class|Mystic": "Mystics follow a strange and rare form of power. They turn inward to master their minds and explore their psyches before facing the world. They can grow huge, bolster militias with fearless resolve, or spy unseen. Most keep their abilities secret.",
 "class|Paladin": "Paladins are bound by oaths to stand against evil. The oath might be sworn at an altar, in a sacred glade, or in grief before only the dead. That bond turns a devout warrior into a blessed champion. They swear to uphold justice and fight darkness wherever it hides.",
 "class|Ranger": "Rangers keep a ceaseless watch in the wilds beyond distant farms. They hunt the monsters that threaten civilization's edges, such as raiders, beasts, giants, and dragons. They track prey like predators, move stealthily, and hide in brush and rubble. Many fight beside animal companions.",
 "class|Rogue": "Rogues rely on skill, stealth, and enemy weaknesses to gain the upper hand. They pick locks, disarm traps, slip into shadows, and lift keys from guards. Their resourcefulness and versatility make them valuable to any party, and they work as hard on their skills as on their combat.",
 "class|Expert Sidekick": "The Expert is a master of particular tasks or knowledge who favors cunning over strength. It could be a scout, musician, librarian, street kid, wily merchant, or burglar. This sidekick leans on skill and know-how.",
 "class|Spellcaster Sidekick": "A sidekick who takes this path follows the ways of magic. It might be a hedge wizard, priest, soothsayer, magical performer, or someone with magic in the blood. This sidekick follows the arcane or divine path.",
 "class|Warrior Sidekick": "A Warrior sidekick grows in fighting skill while it battles beside you. It could be a soldier, town guard, trained beast, or any creature honed for combat. This sidekick suits the front line.",
 "class|Sorcerer": "Sorcerers have magic in their blood, from a strange bloodline, an otherworldly influence, or cosmic forces. You cannot study sorcery like a language, because the power chooses the sorcerer. The magic fills body, mind, and spirit, and its appearance is wildly unpredictable.",
 "class|Warlock": "Warlocks seek hidden knowledge in the fabric of the multiverse. A pact with a mysterious being, such as a fey noble, demon, devil, hag, or Far Realm entity, grants their magic. Patrons are not gods. The bond often resembles master and apprentice, and the patron asks for occasional services.",
 "class|Wizard": "Wizards are supreme spellcasters, united by the spells they cast. They draw on the weave of magic that fills the cosmos for fire, lightning, deception, and mind control. Their magic can summon monsters, glimpse the future, raise zombies, call meteors, and open portals to other worlds.",
 "sub|Path of the Ancestral Guardian": "Barbarians of this path call on the spirits of their ancestors to protect allies and punish enemies. Their rage opens a bridge to the departed, who stand guard over the living. They fight to honor family and lineage.",
 "sub|Path of the Storm Herald": "Barbarians of this path carry a raging storm within them. Their fury unleashes a swirling aura of nature's weather, and each rage takes on the character of the tempest they choose. They fight as living storms.",
 "sub|College of Glamour": "Bards of this college wield fey allure and enchantment. They enthrall crowds with beauty and charm, and their magic bends attention and affection toward them and their allies. Their illusions dazzle and delight.",
 "sub|College of Whispers": "Bards of this college trade in secrets and fear. They gather hidden knowledge, plant dread in the minds of enemies, and slip words into the ears of the powerful. Their whispers cut deeper than blades.",
 "sub|Forge Domain": "Clerics of this domain serve gods of craft and creation. They honor the hammer and the flame, making and strengthening items with divine fire. Their faith values skilled work and the sturdy things it produces.",
 "sub|Grave Domain": "Clerics of this domain watch over the line between life and death. They respect the dead, see that the dying find rest, and oppose undeath. Their magic guards the natural cycle of mortal lives.",
 "sub|Arcana Domain": "Clerics of this domain see magic and the divine as one harmony, like colors in a vast cosmic painting. They serve gods of magic and blend arcane lore with holy power.",
 "sub|Circle of Dreams": "Druids of this circle draw on the gentle realm of dreams and the Feywild. They soothe, heal, and protect with a restful, twilight kind of magic. Their power comes from the soft beauty of the fey.",
 "sub|Arcane Archer": "Fighters of this tradition infuse their arrows with magic. Elven archers long guarded the secret, training for years to shoot with supernatural skill. Each shot can carry a special magical effect to fell distant foes.",
 "sub|Way of the Kensei": "Monks of this tradition train with weapons as if they were extensions of their own bodies. They pursue mastery of the blade and brush with the same discipline as their martial arts. Their approach joins art and combat.",
 "sub|Way of the Sun Soul": "Monks of this tradition channel their ki into radiant energy. They hurl bolts of searing light and burn with inner brilliance. Their spirit shines out as a weapon against darkness.",
 "sub|Warrior of the Mystic Arts": "Fists can be powerful, and magic makes them more so. Monks of this path add spellcasting to their martial training and strike with arcane force alongside their unarmed blows. Their discipline joins the body and the arcane.",
 "sub|Oath of Conquest": "Paladins of this oath seek to crush resistance and impose order through strength. They inspire dread in enemies and command others with iron will. Their goal is victory that leaves no room for rebellion.",
 "sub|Oath of Redemption": "Paladins of this oath believe in peace and in giving even wrongdoers a chance to change. They try to end conflict without violence, and protect the innocent. Their path is mercy first and force only when needed.",
 "sub|Gloom Stalker": "Rangers of this conclave hunt in darkness and shadow. They ambush foes in dim places, strike first, and vanish. They are masters of fear and the night, and dark corners are their hunting ground.",
 "sub|Horizon Walker": "Rangers of this conclave guard the planar borders against otherworldly threats. They step between places in an instant and strike through the gaps between planes. They ward the world from invaders from beyond.",
 "sub|Mastermind": "Rogues of this archetype are schemers who rely on intrigue and insight. They read people, plan carefully, and help allies from behind the scenes. Information and influence are their greatest tools.",
 "sub|Swashbuckler": "Rogues of this archetype fight with flair, fast footwork, and a dash of charm. They duel with daring and style, and enjoy the spotlight. A swashbuckler turns every fight into a performance.",
 "sub|Divine Soul": "Sorcerers of this bloodline carry a spark of divinity. Their magic comes from a heavenly or infernal source, and they can draw on spells from the divine as well as the arcane. Their wings, when they appear, mark their nature.",
 "sub|Shadow Magic": "Sorcerers of this origin draw power from the Shadowfell. Darkness, fear, and the whispers of the dead answer their call. They are tied to shadow, and sometimes it seems to move on its own.",
 "sub|Storm Sorcery": "Sorcerers of this origin command wind, lightning, and thunder. The fury of the sky flows through them, letting them ride the gale and strike like a tempest. Their power is the weather itself.",
 "sub|The Hexblade": "Warlocks of this patron bind themselves to a mysterious, sentient weapon from the Shadowfell. The blade grants them martial skill and curses their enemies. Its will is dark and its bargains costly.",
 "sub|Vestige Patron": "The multiverse holds many gods, and not all have names in temple halls. Warlocks of this patron commune with the benevolence of a forgotten god. Theirs is a noble pursuit of an almost lost kindness.",
 "sub|War Magic": "Wizards of this tradition blend offense and defense, trained for the battlefield. They shield themselves while striking foes, and think tactically. Their spells serve generals and soldiers alike, and fit a mind built for war.",
 "sub|Conjurer": "In the Weave, physical distance means nothing. Wizards of this school learn that with enough power they can travel anywhere in existence by thought alone, and summon what they need to their side.",
 "sub|Enchanter": "Minds can be shaped like clay when magic is at work. Wizards of this school charm and sway others. They are warned to take care, because such power is easy to abuse.",
 "sub|Necromancer": "To the most powerful mages, life and death are interchangeable states. Wizards of this school study the boundary between them, wielding energies of the grave and calling on the dead to serve.",
 "sub|Transmuter": "Wizards of this school commune with the Weave until the limits of the body begin to fall away. They change matter and form, reshaping their surroundings and themselves, treating matter as something to be reworked.",
}
